# ============================================================================
# EVAL SHEET: "Camera's position and direction" — camera on the x-axis
# ============================================================================
# Requirement (verbatim): "Generate a random scene and place the camera
# extending along the x-axis, pointed towards the coordinates {0, 0, 0}, and
# display the rendered image. The scene must be visible and displayed
# without glitching."
# Same small "random" object cluster is reused across files 09-12 (only the
# camera line changes) so any glitch is provably about the camera axis, not
# about the scene contents differing between runs.

#ambient strength/ratio RGB_col( , , )
A 0.2 255,255,255

#camera pos( , , ) camera_dir( , , ) field_of_view(in deg)
# Position sits purely on the x-axis (y=0, z=0); direction (-1,0,0) points
# straight back along -x, i.e. at the origin.
C 16,0,0 -1,0,0 60

#L pos( , , ) brightness_ratio RGB_col( , , )
L 6,8,-6 0.8 255,255,255

#sp sphere_center( , , ) diameter RGB_colour( , , )
sp -1,0,1 3 255,60,60

#pl point_on_pl( , , ) normal_vector( , , ) RGB_colour( , , )
pl 0,-3,0 0,1,0 130,130,130

#cy center( , , ) axis_vector( , , ) diameter height RGB_colour( , , )
cy 2,-1,-1 0,1,0 1.5 4 60,140,255
